@startuml
!include ../themes/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' SPEC: _spec/_plans/chess-analytics.puml
' purpose: StarChess analytics reads StarChessGameRecord.result — it does not re-score
' status: proposed 2026-09-17, not implemented; product = StarChess
' covers: apps/starchess/src/store/matchHistoryStore.ts
'         apps/starchess/src/types/review.ts
'         apps/starchess/src/screens/ReviewScreen.tsx
' live spec: _spec/apps/starchess/replay-import.puml
'   outcome mapping it must wait on ..... _spec/_plans/forfeit-as-loss.puml
'   export as a fixture source .......... _spec/_plans/game-export-localstorage.puml
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' ── WHAT THE LINE ITEM SETTLES ─────────────────────────────────────────────
' Analytics is a READ MODEL over finished StarChess games. Wins, losses,
' draws, forfeits-as-losses, maybe opponent script. It does not decide a
' winner and does not call ""scOutcome"" / ""endScTurn"" again.
'
' ── WHAT IT DOES NOT SETTLE ────────────────────────────────────────────────
'   Coach gameHistoryStore dashboards (different product)
'   which charts, which time window
'   whether tutorials count
title PLANNED — analytics is a read model;\nit does not re-score a match

database "StarChessGameRecord\nresult · opponent" as GAMES <<db>>
component "tally / read model" as TALLY <<app>>
component "Review list / summary" as DASH <<app>>
component "forfeit → loss mapping" as MAP <<app>>
component "**re-resolve SCFEN**\nfights the engine" as RESCORE <<error>>

GAMES ARROW_MAIN TALLY
MAP ARROW_MAIN GAMES : writes the enum
TALLY ARROW_MAIN DASH
TALLY ARROW_ERROR RESCORE

note bottom of RESCORE
  **Charts must not replay StarChess,
  because walking ""resolves"" to decide
  a winner forks the dashboard on a
  rules patch.** Count ""result"".
end note

note bottom of MAP
  **Leave-as-loss has to land before
  tallies, because counts built against
  a void jump when concede becomes a
  loss.** Snapshot after that write.
end note

note right of DASH
  **First surface is the Review list
  plus a summary row, not a new app.**
  Group on ""opponent"" (naive |
  strategic), not a Coach elo enum.
end note

legend bottom
  **The order to do it in**
  ==
  **1. After forfeit-as-loss.** Confirm
  ""StarChessMatchResult"", then define
  tallies: games, wins, losses (including
  leave), draws, by ""opponent"" if present.
  --
  **2. Read, do not replay.** The dashboard
  binds to the tally. Export files can
  backfill; a dump is a fixture, not a
  second scorer.
  ==
  **3. Stay on Review chrome.** Fancy
  charts are a later slice and still
  consume the same tally.
  --
  **Left open**: time windows; whether
  arena imports count; tutorial games.
end legend
@enduml
